codex
§3 is right on the main fact: DMA updates `d->dmaaddr` at completion, after advancing by 12 bytes plus the payload length per command. Two details matter for the rest of the review: “differs from the programmed value” does not prove exact field reporting, and an unconditional `odata` assignment before the switch would also change other registers’ default read values.

codex
The proposed detector also needs to check normal return and absence of the read diagnostic. Keeping `fatal(...)` can pass both value checks if it returns. `MAPLE_STATE == 0` cannot independently prove DMA completion: that register always reads zero, including after an early return.

codex
VERDICT: The read-arm correction can proceed independently. §3’s state trace is correct; its observability claim needs qualification, and the proposed detector is insufficient.
